#
# Per-rig overrides for the ain subprocess.
#
# Sourced from config/ainconf.tcl at the end of its startup, so the
# dserv_ain module is loaded and ainSetNchan has already run. Use this file
# for anything rig-specific: enabling acquisition, non-default channel count,
# signal inversions, or a custom dpoint prefix if this rig wants to isolate
# its ain output.
#
# NOTE: acquisition is OFF by default — host-side analog input now lives on
# the extio box. Only enable it here if this rig genuinely has an MCP320x on
# the host SPI bus. "hardware 1" in ainGetInfo only means /dev/spidev0.0
# opened, NOT that a chip is answering; starting acquisition against an empty
# bus costs ~67% of a core on an i.MX93 and pins slider/position at -2048.
#

# Enable acquisition at 1 kHz (this rig has a real host-side MCP320x).
#
# ainStart 1

# Example: run at 500 Hz instead of 1 kHz.
# If acquisition is already running, ainStop first.
#
# ainStart 2

# Example: invert channel 1 (signal maps 4095..0 instead of 0..4095).
# Useful if the pot is wired "backwards" from what the experiment
# expects.
#
# ainInvertSignal 1 1

# Example: change the output prefix so this rig's ain module publishes
# to "foo/vals" instead of "ain/vals". Leave commented out to keep the
# default (which is what the slider subprocess subscribes to).
#
# ainSetPrefix foo

# Print a summary of the resulting state so the log clearly shows what
# this rig is configured for.
puts "ain (local): [ainGetInfo]"
